Then Jesus walked a little further. And while he was doing this, he saw James, the son of Zebedee, and his brother John. They were in a boat preparing their nets.
Immediately he called them. They left father Zebedee in the boat with the hired men. Then they followed Jesus. Jesus Expels an Unclean Spirit
Jesus and those who were with him went to Capernaum. When the Sabbath came, he went to the synagogue. There he began to teach.
People were astonished at his teaching. He taught them as one having authority, and not as the scribes.
Suddenly, a man in their temple screamed. He was under the control of an evil spirit. He said:
"What do you want from us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are. You are the Holy One of God!"
Jesus said firmly, "Stop talking!" "Come out of him!"
The evil spirit shook the man violently. Then it came out of him with a scream.
Everyone was astonished. They asked one another, "What is this? A new teaching! And with such authority! He even gives orders to evil spirits, and they obey him."
News about Jesus spread quickly throughout Galilee. Jesus heals many people.
Jesus and those with him went out from the synagogue. Immediately they went with James and John to the house of Simon and Andrew.
Simon's mother-in-law was lying in bed. She was suffering from a fever. They told Jesus about her condition.
When he went to her, he took her hand and helped her up. He recovered her from the fever. After that, she began to serve them.
That evening, after sunset, the people brought to Jesus all who were sick. They also brought all who were possessed by demons.
All the people in the town gathered at the door.
Jesus healed many people. They had all kinds of diseases. He also drove out many demons. But he did not let the demons speak, because they knew who he was. Jesus prays in a quiet place.
It was very early in the morning and still dark. Jesus got up and went out of the house. He went to a place where he could be alone. There he prayed.
Simon and his friends went to look for Jesus.
When they found him, they shouted, "Everyone is looking for you!"
Jesus replied, "Let's go somewhere else. I want to go to the nearby towns. I must preach there also. That is why I came."
He traveled everywhere in Galilee, preaching in their synagogues, also casting out demons. Jesus heals a man who had a skin disease.
A man who had a skin disease came to Jesus. On his knees he asked Jesus. He said, "If you want to make me "clean", you can do it."
Jesus was filled with profound anxiety. He reached out and touched the man. "I am willing to do this," he said. "Be 'pure'!"
Immediately, he left the illness. He was cured.
Then Jesus quickly sent him away. The man was given a strong warning.
He said, "Don't tell anyone that," "Go and present yourself to the priest. Make the sacrifices that Moses commanded. He will be a witness to the priest and the people that you are 'clean'."
But the man went out and began to talk directly. He spread the news to all the people. So Jesus could no longer enter the city publicly. He stayed outside in secluded places. But people still came to him from everywhere.
Jesus heals a man who could not walk.
A few days later, Jesus entered Capernaum again. The people heard that he had returned home.
The crowd grew so large that there was no more room. Not even outside the door was there any more room. And Jesus spoke to them, saying, "The words I speak to you are spirit and they are life."
Four of those who came were carrying a man who could not walk.
But they couldn't bring him near Jesus because of the crowd. So they went up to the roof where Jesus was and opened up a hole in the ceiling above Jesus. Then they lowered the man on his stretcher through the hole.
Jesus saw their faith. He said to the man, "Son, your sins are forgiven."
Some of the law professors were sitting there. They were thinking.
Why does he say that? He's saying something terrible! Only God can forgive sins!
Immediately Jesus knew in his spirit what they were thinking, and he said to them, "Why are you thinking these things in your hearts?"
Is it easier to tell him, "Your sins are forgiven"? Or to say, "Rise, take up your bed, and walk"?
"I want you to know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins." Then Jesus spoke to the man who could not walk.
He said, "I'm telling you, get up. Take your rug and go back to your house."
The man stood up and took his mat. Then he walked away while everyone was watching. Everyone was amazed. They praised God and said, "We have never seen anything like this!" Jesus Chooses Lazarus
Again Jesus went out beside the Sea of Galilee. A great crowd came to him. He began to teach them.
And as for how he was walking, he saw Lawi-`E, the son of Alfaa'i. Lawi-'E was sitting at the desk of the tax collector of the offices. Jesus said to him, "Follow me." Lawi-'E rose up and followed him.
Later, Jesus was having dinner at Levi's house. Many tax collectors and "sinners" were eating with him and his disciples. They were part of the large crowd that was following Jesus.
Some of the teachers of the law who were Pharisees were there. They saw Jesus eating with "sinners" and tax collectors. So they asked his disciples, "Why does he eat with tax collectors and 'sinners'?"
Jesus heard that. He said to them, "Those who are healthy do not need a physician; the sick do. I did not come for those who believe that they are righteous before God to come to me. I came for sinners to follow me." Jesus is asked about fasting.
The disciples of John and of the Pharisees used to fast. Some people came to Jesus and said, "The disciples of John fast, and the disciples of the Pharisees fast. But your disciples do not fast. Why is this?"
Jesus answered, "How can the guests of the bridegroom fast while he is with them? As long as he is with them, they cannot fast.
But the time will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them; and in that day they shall go out unto the mountains weeping, and lamenting in every bed.
People don't patch a new piece of cloth onto old clothes. If they did, the new piece would stick out from the old. Thus, the tear would increase.
The people do not put new wine into old wineskins. If they do, the wine will burst the wineskins. Then the wine is ruined, and so are the wineskins. No, the people all put new wine into new wineskins." The Lord is the Sabbath."
One Saturday, Jesus was walking with His disciples through fields of grain. His disciples began breaking off some of the heads of grain.
The Pharisees said to Jesus, "Look! It is against the law to do this on the Sabbath. Why do your disciples do this?"
He said, "Haven't you read what David did? He and his men were hungry. They were in need of food."
That was when Abiathar was high priest. David entered the house of God and ate the holy bread. Only the priests were allowed to eat it. He also gave some to his men."
Jesus said to them, "The Sabbath was made for man, not man for the Sabbath."
So the Son of Man is lord even of the Sabbath."
Healing on Saturday
When Jesus went again to the synagogue, there was a man whose hand was withered and deformed.
Some Pharisees were trying to find fault with Jesus. They were observing him closely. They wanted to go where he would perform healings on the Sabbath day.
Jesus said to the man with the withered and deformed hand, "Stand up in front of everyone."
Jesus asked them, "What does the Law say we must do on the Sabbath? Should we do good? Or should we do evil? Should we save life? Or should we kill?" But no one answered.
Jesus looked around at them angrily. He was very upset because their hearts were hardened. Then He said to the man, "Stretch out your hand." He stretched it out, and his hand was as good as new.
Then the Pharisees went out and began to plot with the Herodians against Jesus. A crowd is following Jesus.
Then Jesus went with his disciples to the Sea of Galilee. A great crowd from Galilee followed him.
We hear about all that Jesus was doing. And many people came to him. They came from Judea, Jerusalem, and Edom. They came from the territories east of the Jordan River. And they came from the area around Tyre and Sidon.
Because of the crowd, Jesus told his disciples to bring him a small boat. This would prevent people from crowding him.
Jesus had healed many people. The sick would rush to touch him.
People who had evil spirits in them were there. When they saw Jesus, they fell down in front of him. The spirits yelled, "You are the Son of God!"
But Jesus commanded them not to tell who he was. Jesus appoints the twelve apostles.
Jesus went up a mountain. He called some people to come to him, and they came.
He appointed 12 of them and named them apostles. From then on they would be with him. He would also send them out to preach.
They have authority to expel demons.
Therefore Jesus appointed the twelve. Simon was one of them. Jesus gave him the name Peter.
There was James, the son of Zebedee, and his brother John. Jesus gave them the name Boanerges. Boanerges means Sons of Thunder.
And there were also Andrew, Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, and James the son of Alphaeus. And there were also Thaddaeus and Simon the Zealot.
Jadus Iscariot was one of them too. He was the one who would give you after giving Jesus to his enemy. Jesus and Belial.
Jesus entered a house. A crowd gathered a second time. It was so large that even Jesus and his disciples were unable to eat.
His family heard about this. So they went to take care of him. They said, "He's crazy."
Some of the teachers of the law were there. They had come down from Jerusalem. They said, "He is controlled by Beelzebul! He is driving out demons by the power of the prince of demons."
And he called their Jesus and said to them in parables. He said, "How can a demon cast out a demon?"
If a kingdom fights against itself, it cannot stand.
If a family is divided, it cannot stand.
